 and mind entering the central channel <term>avadhuti</term>;
Bliss from the flowing stream of the mind of enlightenment <term>bodhicitta</term>;
Bliss from the lower parts being pervaded by the refined vital drop;
Bliss from being pervaded by stainless joy;
Bliss from the dawning of the clear light in the mind;
These are the six types of bliss.
These are the six essential points to be practiced.
They dawned in the mind of me, the yogi Repa.
This gathering of joy is a rare occasion.
The beer turns into nectar for you, my good friends.
I, the old man, sing this old song,
To honor you, my disciples.
May this gift of Dharma at this time
Bring joy to the hearts of all who are seated here.
